            "children":[
              {"type":"mol","smiles":"O=[N+]([O-])c1ccc(N2CCN(C(=O)OC(C)(C)C)CC2)cc2C(CCC3(CCC3)O3)=C2","children":[
                {
                  "type":"reaction",
                  "template_id":"R003", // nitration
                  "children":[
                    {"type":"mol","smiles":"c1ccc(N2CCN(C(=O)OC(C)(C)C)CC2)cc2C(CCC3(CCC3)O3)=C2","children":[
                      {
                        "type":"reaction",
                        "template_id":"R004", // Buchwald coupling
                        "children":[
                          {"type":"mol","smiles":"Brc1ccc2c(c1)C(CCC3(CCC3)O3)=C2"},
                          {"type":"mol","smiles":"C(=O)(OC(C)(C)C)N1CCNCC1"}
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "type":"reaction",
                        "template_id":"R005", // bromination
                        "children":[
                          {"type":"mol","smiles":"OC1CCc2ccccc2C1"},
                          {"type":"mol","smiles":"BrBr"}
                        ]
                      }
                    ]}
                  ]
                },
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"Cl[Sn](Cl)"} // reducing agent
              ]
            ]
          }
        ]}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

But need to ensure each reaction's children are only molecules (type mol). The nested children inside a mol node may not be allowed per schema? The schema expects that a mol node can have children (reactions) maybe? The description: root is a molecule with children that are either reactions or other molecules. So a mol can have a reaction child. So we can embed reaction under mol.

Thus we can structure as:

Target mol -> reaction (sulfonylation) -> children: sulfonyl chloride (mol), aniline intermediate (mol). The aniline intermediate mol has child reaction (reduction) etc.

Thus we need to embed reaction nodes as children of mol nodes.

Let's construct final JSON accordingly.

Make sure no comments, no trailing commas.

